**Amendment (Engineering measurements and conformance)** · `amend:devperf:measurement-claim-scope` Under (`rule:devperf:scope`) and (`rule:testing:public-record-conformance`), measured CPU, wall time, load, availability and numerical Work are scoped engineering observations, not protocol capacities. Their recorded samples and arithmetic can be checked; the public bytes do not independently attest sampling, hardware or elapsed time. A Work measurement also names the numerical build and procedure under (`rule:design:build-relative-work`); a dependency upgrade neither carries a prior count forward as a new measurement nor changes the verdict of a certificate. This changes no budget, threshold or measurement value.
